    "topic": "The barcode started as a drawing in the sand",
    "summary": "Norman Joseph Woodland formed his first barcode from sand on a beach in Florida, extending Morse code's dots and dashes downwards into narrow and wide lines. He and Bernard Silver filed a patent on 20 October 1949, issued 7 October 1952. On 26 June 1974, a 10-pack of Wrigley's Juicy Fruit gum was scanned at Marsh's Supermarket in Troy, Ohio, the first commercial use of the UPC.",
